.SS "WORD stumpless_get_wel_category (const struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * entry)"

.PP
Gets the category of an entry used with Windows Event Log targets\&. The category is used by a Windows Event Log target\&. Entries that are going to be sent to a Windows Event Log target must have the category specified before they are sent\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&. A mutex is used to coordinate changes to the entry and its WEL data while it is being modified\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate changes\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIentry\fP The entry to get the category from\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The entry category\&. In the event of an error, then zero is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

